# user memory (loads in every project). Do NOT rely on this copy in the repo as
# active memory — it lives here only as a shareable starting point.

## General workflow
- Prefer `pip install -e ".[dev]"` (or `uv pip install -e ".[dev]"`) for setup.
- Use `ruff` for lint+format, `pytest` for tests, `mypy` (strict) for types.
- Explain non-obvious decisions in one line; show diffs before applying them.
- Ask before running anything destructive (`rm -rf`, force-push, history rewrite).

## AgentRail-specific personal notes
- Default to `plan` mode when exploring an unfamiliar subsystem.
- When testing tmux code locally, use a dedicated socket so it never touches my
  real tmux server:
  `libtmux.Server(socket_name="agentrail_dev")`.
- Isolated worktrees live under `.agentrail/worktrees/<stage-id>/`; runtime state
  under `.agentrail/` is gitignored — don't commit it.
- Verify model IDs against provider docs before pinning; they rotate often (the
  effort-tier → model_id mapping lives in agentrail/profiles config).
- Canonical smoke test:
  `agentrail plan "Implement login and logout as separate PRs"` then `status`.

